The five-step method
STEP 1 — SYMBOLS: assign letters (dominant capital: A; recessive lowercase: a) and state what each means. STEP 2 — PARENTS: write both genotypes with phenotypes (e.g. Aa tall × aa short). STEP 3 — GAMETES: list each parent's possible gametes (Aa makes A and a; aa makes only a). STEP 4 — SQUARE: draw the Punnett grid, fill every box. STEP 5 — RATIOS: state genotype ratio AND phenotype ratio (or probabilities). TEST CROSS: to reveal an unknown dominant phenotype (A? ), cross with homozygous recessive (aa) — if ANY recessive offspring appear, the parent was heterozygous; if dozens of offspring are all dominant, it is almost certainly AA. PEDIGREES: dominant traits appear every generation (affected children always have an affected parent); recessive traits skip generations and appear from carrier parents; if two normal parents have an affected child, the trait MUST be recessive.$wdthseed$, NULL, 40, 2, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Apply the five-step cross method to any monohybrid problem","Use test crosses to reveal unknown genotypes","Read simple pedigrees for dominant and recessive traits"],"introduction":"Genetics problems look frightening until you learn the method. With five disciplined steps, every monohybrid cross — in homework, WAEC or JAMB — surrenders.","key_points":["Never skip the gamete step","Test crosses use homozygous recessive partners","Pedigree rules beat pedigree guessing"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 12 (monohybrid crosses, pedigrees)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod05$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod05:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.cont