Three dominance patterns
COMPLETE DOMINANCE: heterozygote matches one parent (Tt peas are tall). INCOMPLETE DOMINANCE: heterozygote is INTERMEDIATE — red snapdragon (CRCR) × white (CWCW) gives all pink (CRCW); self-crossing pinks gives 1 red : 2 pink : 1 white (note: use SUPERSCRIPT letters, never Rr, to avoid implying dominance). CODOMINANCE: heterozygote shows BOTH traits fully — roan cattle (red + white hairs), and human AB blood (both A and B antigens). MULTIPLE ALLELES: more than two alleles exist in the population — ABO blood has THREE (IA, IB, i): IA and IB are codominant with each other, both dominant over i. Genotypes: group A = IAIA or IAi; B = IBIB or IBi; AB = IAIB; O = ii (universal donor — no antigens; AB is universal recipient — no antibodies).

Sickle cell: dominance depends on the level
Sickle-cell anaemia shows dominance beautifully: at the MOLECULAR level, HbAHbS carriers make both normal and sickle haemoglobin (codominance); at the ORGANISM level in normal air, carriers look healthy (recessive disease); under severe oxygen shortage, carriers can show symptoms (incomplete dominance). One gene, three answers — dominance describes RELATIONSHIPS, not alleles alone. In malaria regions, carriers survive best (heterozygote advantage — the final-exam favourite), keeping the HbS allele common despite the disease. Genetic counselling lets carrier couples understand their 1-in-4 risk per pregnancy.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 3, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Distinguish complete, incomplete and codominance","Explain ABO blood groups as multiple alleles + codominance","Predict safe blood transfusions from donor and recipient groups"],"introduction":"Red snapdragon × white snapdragon gives... pink. Neither allele dominates — Mendel's rules still apply, but dominance itself has shades.","key_points":["Superscripts for incomplete dominance (CRCW)","ABO genotypes must be memorised","O donates, AB receives"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 12 (extensions of Mendel)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod05$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod05:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_