The equation
PHOTOSYNTHESIS: carbon dioxide + water → (light energy + chlorophyll) → glucose + oxygen. Symbol: 6CO2 + 6H2O → C6H12O6 + 6O2. It happens in CHLOROPLASTS: chlorophyll traps light, splitting water (photolysis — releasing the O2 we breathe) and fixing CO2 into glucose via the Calvin cycle. Glucose is then: RESPIRED for energy (plants respire day and night), CONVERTED to STARCH for storage (tubers, seeds), built into CELLULOSE for walls, combined with nitrates into AMINO ACIDS/PROTEINS, or stored as OILS (palm fruit, groundnut). Without photosynthesis there is no food chain, no oxygen atmosphere, no fossil fuel — every meal and every breath begins here.

Leaf adaptations
Leaves are optimised on five fronts. (1) BROAD and THIN: huge area catches light; short diffusion paths move gases fast. (2) CHLOROPHYLL packed in palisade mesophyll near the upper surface — most light meets most pigment. (3) STOMATA (pores, mostly underneath) + AIR SPACES let CO2 diffuse in and O2 out; guard cells open/close them to balance gas entry against water loss. (4) VEINS (xylem + phloem) deliver water and export sugars while stiffening the blade. (5) WAXY CUTICLE cuts evaporation while staying transparent. Desert plants modify the plan (spines, sunken stomata, CAM night-photosynthesis); water plants float stomata on top. Examination pattern: adaptation → feature → benefit ('stomata allow CO2 entry for photosynthesis').$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 1, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Write the word and symbol equations for photosynthesis","Explain five leaf adaptations","State the uses of glucose in plants"],"introduction":"A cassava leaf turns sunlight, air and water into the garri on your table. No factory on Earth matches it — and it runs silently, for free, while cleaning the air.","key_points":["Both equations from memory","Five adaptations as feature → benefit","Glucose has five fates"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 8, Photosynthesis"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod09:top01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
